149	  // that ledger window is a sub-second internal transient, too narrow to
150	  // observe reliably from a cross-process e2e poll, so here we assert the
151	  // user-visible journey rather than the ledger's internals.
152	  //
153	  // Foreground the friend first: unlike RECEIVING the host's edit (network
154	  // callbacks fire while occluded), the friend's OWN break is engine-rAF-driven,
155	  // and the browser throttles rAF hard on a backgrounded page (the friend has
156	  // sat behind the host all along), so occluded its mining crawls and can miss
157	  // the 45s window. Foregrounded, its engine steps at full rate. (bringToFront
158	  // alone once looked like it broke digging — that was the airborne-aim miss the
159	  // onGround wait in forceDigStraightDown now covers, not bringToFront itself.)
